@startuml process-restart-recovery
!include state-machine-style.iuml
title Slop Machine | Process restart recovery (proposal)
caption Startup classifies every persisted task before its scheduler dispatch is enabled.

state "Start with dispatch paused\nNo new claims or agent assignments" as Boot
state "Establish coordinator ownership\nDurable epoch/lock; reject old-epoch writes" as Own
state "Load recovery inventory\nCheckpoints, claims/slots, journal, outbox,\nsessions, volume refs and external intents" as Load
state Kind <<choice>>

state "Restore passive task\nQueued, waiting or terminal; no live run" as Restore <<success>>
state "Reconcile pending outcome sync\nNo slot; read Jira/task before retry" as Sync
state SyncResult <<choice>>
state "Outcome sync restored\nEffect confirmed or safe retry completed" as SyncDone <<success>>
state "Quarantine task or sync\nMissing evidence or unresolved effect\nDo not silently reschedule" as Quarantine <<attention>>

state "Isolate interrupted active run\nKeep claim/slot; block task volume" as Isolate
state "Stop or fence prior executors\nRevoke session/tool authority\nConfirm no surviving volume writer" as Fence
state Fenced <<choice>>
state "Reconcile in-flight operations\nCompare intent, checkpoint, journal and\nobserved Git, PR, Jira/provider effects" as Reconcile
state Effect <<choice>>
state "Verify run boundary\nVolume/clone, task/spec/config, selected access, budget\nConfirmed effects applied to workflow state" as Verify
state SafeToResume <<choice>>
state "Start replacement task container\nMount SAME run volume; keep claim and slot\nFetch current selected credential from manager\nSee access-readiness.puml: replacement_start" as ReplaceWorker
state "Resume SAME run at saved stage\nFresh sessions + explicit context; new invocation IDs\nRecheck policy before new work" as Resume <<success>>
state "End interrupted run\nRecord partial/unknown effects and reason\nRetire safe volume or retain dirty manifest\nSync attention/cancellation as needed" as EndRun
state EndResult <<choice>>
state "Old run safely closed\nRelease claim/slot; later pickup gets\nNEW run and NEW volume/full clone" as Closed <<attention>>
state "Recovery blocked\nWriter or cleanup ownership uncertain\nKeep claim/slot; no new executor" as Blocked <<attention>>
state "Global startup blocked\nStore or coordinator ownership unproven\nNo scheduling" as GlobalBlock <<attention>>

[*] --> Boot
Boot --> Own
Own --> Load : single current owner established
Own --> GlobalBlock : old writer cannot be excluded
Load --> Kind : inventory readable and consistent enough to classify
Load --> GlobalBlock : required store unreadable/corrupt
Kind --> Restore : [queued/waiting/terminal; no pending effect]
Kind --> Sync : [run ended; outcome sync pending]
Kind --> Isolate : [claim, run, cleanup or operation in flight]
Kind --> Quarantine : [record inconsistent/missing evidence]
Sync --> SyncResult : remote/internal state checked
SyncResult --> SyncDone : [effect confirmed or safe retry]
SyncResult --> Quarantine : [effect unresolved]
Isolate --> Fence
Fence --> Fenced : prior process/session/lease checked
Fenced --> Reconcile : [all prior executors stopped/fenced]
Fenced --> Blocked : [writer could still act]
Reconcile --> Effect : every pending operation classified
Effect --> Verify : [effects confirmed or absence proven]
Effect --> EndRun : [effect still unknown] / no blind replay
Verify --> SafeToResume : current inputs and boundary assessed
Verify --> Blocked : volume/clone ownership cannot be established
SafeToResume --> ReplaceWorker : [consistent checkpoint; valid workspace,\ninputs, selected mode and budget]
SafeToResume --> EndRun : [stale, unsafe, cancelled or no valid boundary]
ReplaceWorker --> Resume : current credential + runtime ready;\ncheckpoint and volume/clone still match
ReplaceWorker --> EndRun : credential or runtime unavailable\nafter bounded recovery; no agent work resumed
EndRun --> EndResult : cleanup and outcome recorded
EndResult --> Closed : [safe retirement or recorded retention]
EndResult --> Blocked : [cleanup/ownership unconfirmed]

Restore --> [*]
SyncDone --> [*]
Quarantine --> [*]
Resume --> [*]
Closed --> [*]
Blocked --> [*]
GlobalBlock --> [*]

note right of Reconcile
  A timeout or expired lease never proves the prior effect absent.
  Match stable operation IDs and external evidence before retry.
  Confirmed effects advance the state; no old tool call is replayed.
  Jira Done still requires verified target-branch publication.
end note
note bottom of Resume
  Same-run recovery keeps the existing volume, clone and slot. The
  replacement container fetches a fresh current credential;
  saved token bytes are never restored. Lost agent sessions are
  rebuilt from durable context, findings and code snapshot.
  Resume only at a verified workflow boundary, not mid-command.
end note
note bottom of Closed
  Each task is classified before dispatch opens for it.
  Other eligible tasks may proceed while one remains blocked.
  An unfenced writer keeps its slot; a fenced, closed run does not.
end note
@enduml
